{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible-light-mediated direct deoxygenative C-C coupling of aromatic carboxylic acids with alkenes to synthesize ketones. Using triphenylphosphine as an oxygen-transfer reagent and an iridium photocatalyst, the method avoids the need for pre-activating acids into acid chlorides or anhydrides. The reaction is compatible with aqueous conditions and various biomolecules, enabling late-stage functionalization of pharmaceuticals and the synthesis of macrocyclic ketones.",
